@startuml
title UML sequence - account recovery with ownership verification, risk and independent approval
actor Customer
actor Support
actor Approver
participant "bank-api" as API
participant "Controls functions" as C
participant "Issuer (bank-identity-admin)" as Issuer
participant "Data notifications" as N
Customer -> API : Sign out everywhere (authenticated session)
API -> C : request_recovery(LOST_DEVICE, AUTHENTICATED_SESSION)
C -> C : risk = contact change 7d / open monitoring alert / recovery 30d
C --> API : APPROVED (HIGH risk opens a review case)
API -> Issuer : logout all user sessions (secret read from file)
API -> API : delete server-held browser sessions
API -> C : complete_recovery -> EXECUTED
C -> N : SECURITY notice "Your devices were signed out"
Support -> API : staff recovery(person, CREDENTIAL_RESET, VERIFIED_CONTACT)
API -> C : request_recovery -> PENDING_APPROVAL + SECURITY case
Approver -> API : decision(approve, reason)
API -> C : decide_recovery (approver != requester != customer)
API -> Issuer : logout + required action UPDATE_PASSWORD
API -> C : complete_recovery -> EXECUTED
note right of Issuer : staff never see or set the password;\nthe next login stops at the password update
@enduml
